```typescript
  // Initialize animation clip reference
  // This runs once when actions change, storing the clip for manual sampling
  useEffect(() => {
    const action = actions[clipName];
    if (!action) return;

    // Store the clip for sampling in useFrame
    clipRef.current = action.getClip();

    // Stop the action - we're not using AnimationMixer playback
    // Instead, we manually sample the clip at spring-interpolated times
    action.stop();
  }, [actions, clipName]);
```

## Key Implementation Details

### Why action.stop()?
- We don't use Three.js AnimationMixer for playback
- AnimationMixer doesn't support custom easing functions
- Instead, we manually sample clip values at arbitrary times
- Calling stop() ensures the mixer doesn't interfere with our manual control

### Clip vs Action
- `action`: THREE.AnimationAction - controls playback (play, pause, stop, timeScale)
- `clip`: THREE.AnimationClip - contains keyframe data (tracks, duration)
- We only need the clip for its tracks and duration

### Dependencies
- `actions`: Changes when GLTF loads or animations change
- `clipName`: Allows using same hook for different clips

